        }
      ],
      "content": "of obscure origin; possibly from Rijssel, the Flemish name of Lille. The early forms, and the fact that black and other colors occur earlier and more frequently than red, are against connexion with russel in the sense of ‘reddish’. A kind of woollen fabric (worsted among other things) formerly used for articles of attire, especially in the 16th century (OED s.v. russel²), here broad"
    }
